## Phase 1 — Data pipeline & baseline model  ✅ DONE

**Goal:** a reproducible path from raw dataset to a persisted, evaluated classifier.

Scope:
- Project scaffold, pinned `requirements.txt`, `.gitignore`, README, dataset notes.
- `src/config.py` — single source of truth for paths, seed, feature lists, artefact locations.
- `src/data.py` — download + cache `german.data`; rename columns; decode every `Axx`
  code to a human-readable label; derive the `default` target and the `sex` / `age_group`
  protected attributes used later by the fairness audit.
- `src/preprocess.py` — `ColumnTransformer`: `StandardScaler` on 7 numeric columns,
  dense `OneHotEncoder` on 13 categoricals (dense so SHAP's TreeExplainer can consume it).
- `src/train.py` — `LogisticRegression` vs `XGBoost`, stratified 5-fold CV on the
  training split, refit on full train, evaluate on a 20% hold-out. Persist the model,
  the preprocessor, `model_metadata.json`, `reports/metrics.json`, and 3 diagnostic figures.
- `src/evaluate.py` — threshold-free metrics (ROC-AUC, PR-AUC, Brier) + thresholded
  metrics (precision, recall, F1, confusion matrix) + ROC / PR / confusion-matrix plots.

Deliverables: `models/xgboost_model.joblib`, `models/preprocessor.joblib`,
`models/model_metadata.json`, `reports/metrics.json`, `reports/figures/*.png`.

Exit criteria: `python -m src.train` runs clean; artefacts reload and predict; metrics
recorded. **See `Phases/Phase 1` for the completion report.**

